WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:03.470 align:start position:0%
 
better  internet  foragers is a documentary highlighting  how Israel prevents Palestinians from  picking wild herbs it's one of 24  Palestinian films competing for the  Sunbird award during the Palestine  cinnamonies Festival  voicing visual memory is the festival's  theme this year the festival also aims  to promote Palestinian Film Production  and provide a stage for Palestinian  narratives  no one can tell our story like we can  imagine a Hollywood movie discussing  issues of Native Americans it would be  whitewashing no matter the treatment  narrative or terminology used the most  important question remains who is  producing the image  Palestinians say they are rarely given a  platform to tell their own stories and  when their stories do reach  International audiences it usually  Israeli filmmakers who tell them  participants in this Workshop say  they're reclaiming The Narrative they  take Israeli movies and reconstruct them  from their own perspective what we  wanted to do with these films is not  just to criticize what was wrong and  what was right but rather to to think  how can we say our narrative what is how  can we use these films as an as  important archival material in narrating  our story pro-israeli views still  dominate the public sphere recently  Marvel Studios announced it will feature  an Israeli superhero in the new Captain  America movie it's insulted my  grandmother they may not be Blockbusters  but Palestinians are slowly making their  debuts internationally social media and  celebrities speaking up have given them  a space mainstream media can't or won't  many directors here tell us that while  the Palestinian narrative is being  showcased more on International screens  it still has a long way to go they say  the Israeli film industry has the  funding and access to International red  carpet making it very difficult for  Palestinians to compete  Ibrahim al-jazeera the occupied Westbank

